     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range associated with serious liver injury, and 2000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose. I don't know of a standard indication for it in an adult receiving oral dosing. Normal liver function and kidney function don't make it safe.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than that, I can enter a multimodal regimen. That could include an NSAID if appropriate, or another agent you choose.\n\nIf you think this dose is warranted, for example under a specific protocol, please discuss it with pharmacy or toxicology. It would need to go through your institution's formal override process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
